{"id":"bcd498adc92fd397","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-riesz-representation-dp.md","title":"Riesz Representation (Dirichlet)","display":"thm-riesz-representation-dp — Riesz Representation (Dirichlet)","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-riesz-representation-dp","aliases":["58-thm-riesz-representation-dp"],"display":"thm-riesz-representation-dp — Riesz Representation (Dirichlet)","depends_on":["[[58-df-sobolev-space]]","[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md]]","[[../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-riesz-representation-dp"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-riesz-representation-dp</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-riesz-representation-dp — Riesz Representation (Dirichlet)"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"38c58fda0da62833\" href=\"?note=38c58fda0da62833\" title=\"58-df-sobolev-space\">58-df-sobolev-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"261de7e0269cd7e2\" href=\"?note=261de7e0269cd7e2\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md\">../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"dfd5be6f22b3deb4\" href=\"?note=dfd5be6f22b3deb4\" title=\"../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md\">../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\">\\(n\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\">\\(\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W,H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V\">\\(W,H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\">\\(\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|\\cdot\\|_2\">\\(\\|\\cdot\\|_2\\)</span> are the standard Euclidean topology and norm</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_0^1(\\Omega)\">\\(H_0^1(\\Omega)\\)</span> is the closure of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\">\\(C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\)</span> in the Sobolev space <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"W^{1,2}(\\Omega)\">\\(W^{1,2}(\\Omega)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_D(u,v)\\coloneqq\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\">\\(B_D(u,v)\\coloneqq\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_D(u)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B_D(u,u)}\">\\(\\nu_D(u)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B_D(u,u)}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R}\">\\(+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R}\">\\(|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R}\\)</span> are the standard real scalar operations and norm</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\\subseteq V^{10}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\\subseteq V^{10}\\)</span> are the imported exact predicates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S\\)</span> are the local typed predicates defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}open\\text{-}domain\\text{-}for\\text{-}dp}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\n(\\|x\\|_2&lt;r).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}open\\text{-}domain\\text{-}for\\text{-}dp}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\nn\\in\\omega_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\n(\\|x\\|_2&lt;r).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}hilbert\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(W,\\Omega,n,1,2)\n\\land H=H_0^1(\\Omega)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in H\\;\\left(B_D(u,v)=\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\n\\land B_D(u,v)=B_D(v,u)\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_D,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}hilbert\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(W,\\Omega,n,1,2)\n\\land H=H_0^1(\\Omega)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in H\\;\\left(B_D(u,v)=\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\n\\land B_D(u,v)=B_D(v,u)\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_D,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation\\text{-}dp}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(\nf,H,\\mathbb R,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},\n\\nu_D,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists!u\\in H\\;\\forall v\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(B_D(u,v)=f(v)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation\\text{-}dp}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(\nf,H,\\mathbb R,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},\n\\nu_D,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R})\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\exists!u\\in H\\;\\forall v\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(B_D(u,v)=f(v)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The weak Dirichlet problem is now an exact real-Hilbert specialization of the imported Riesz representation theorem.  The Sobolev carrier, Dirichlet inner product, vector operations, and ten-place bounded-linear predicate are explicit.</li>\n<li>Conventionally <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H^{-1}(\\Omega)=(H_0^1(\\Omega))&#39;\">\\(H^{-1}(\\Omega)=(H_0^1(\\Omega))&#39;\\)</span>; the bounded-linear antecedent is the expanded meaning of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in H^{-1}(\\Omega)\">\\(f\\in H^{-1}(\\Omega)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u \\in H_0^1\">\\(u \\in H_0^1\\)</span> minimizes energy <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\int_\\Omega |\\nabla u|^2 - 2\\langle f, u\\rangle\">\\(\\int_\\Omega |\\nabla u|^2 - 2\\langle f, u\\rangle\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f \\in L^2\">\\(f \\in L^2\\)</span>, the solution is in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H^2 \\cap H_0^1\">\\(H^2 \\cap H_0^1\\)</span> if <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\partial\\Omega\">\\(\\partial\\Omega\\)</span> is <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C^2\">\\(C^2\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Green's function <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G(x,y)\">\\(G(x,y)\\)</span> gives <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u(x) = \\int G(x,y)f(y) dy\">\\(u(x) = \\int G(x,y)f(y) dy\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-sobolev-space","status":"resolved","id":"38c58fda0da62833","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-sobolev-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md","status":"resolved","id":"261de7e0269cd7e2","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md","status":"resolved","id":"dfd5be6f22b3deb4","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-prop-riesz-representation.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\omega_{>0}","display":false},{"tex":"\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n","display":false},{"tex":"W,H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H,f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\|\\cdot\\|_2","display":false},{"tex":"H_0^1(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"W^{1,2}(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"B_D(u,v)\\coloneqq\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu_D(u)\\coloneqq\\sqrt{B_D(u,u)}","display":false},{"tex":"+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R}","display":false},{"tex":"|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\\subseteq V^{10}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}open\\text{-}domain\\text{-}for\\text{-}dp}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\\leftrightarrow{}&\nn\\in\\omega_{>0}\n\\land\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n\n\\land\\Omega\\in\\tau_{\\mathbb R^n}\\\\\n&{}\\land\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall x\\in\\Omega\\;\n(\\|x\\|_2<r).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}dirichlet\\text{-}hilbert\\text{-}data}\\vdash\\\\\n&\\quad\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\leftrightarrow\\\\\n&\\qquad\\mathrm{SobolevSpace}_S(W,\\Omega,n,1,2)\n\\land H=H_0^1(\\Omega)\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in H\\;\\left(B_D(u,v)=\\int_\\Omega\\nabla u\\cdot\\nabla v\n\\land B_D(u,v)=B_D(v,u)\\right)\\\\\n&\\hspace{5em}{}\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(H,B_D,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}riesz\\text{-}representation\\text{-}dp}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{BoundedOpenDomain}_S(\\Omega,\\mathbb R^n)\n\\land\\mathrm{DirichletHilbertData}_S(H,B_D,+_H,\\odot_H;\\Omega,n,W)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S(\nf,H,\\mathbb R,\\mathbb R,+_H,\\odot_H,+_{\\mathbb R},\\cdot_{\\mathbb R},\n\\nu_D,|\\cdot|_{\\mathbb R})\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\\exists!u\\in H\\;\\forall v\\in H\\;\n\\bigl(B_D(u,v)=f(v)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"H^{-1}(\\Omega)=(H_0^1(\\Omega))'","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in H^{-1}(\\Omega)","display":false},{"tex":"u \\in H_0^1","display":false},{"tex":"\\int_\\Omega |\\nabla u|^2 - 2\\langle f, u\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"f \\in L^2","display":false},{"tex":"H^2 \\cap H_0^1","display":false},{"tex":"\\partial\\Omega","display":false},{"tex":"C^2","display":false},{"tex":"G(x,y)","display":false},{"tex":"u(x) = \\int G(x,y)f(y) dy","display":false}],"bytes":3080,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4396","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-riesz-representation-dp.md|58-thm-riesz-representation-dp]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["38c58fda0da62833","b70ce791d5b1a19b","261de7e0269cd7e2","dfd5be6f22b3deb4"]}